(4976811, 722920, 38032, '<td valign="top">First of all: Avoid pointing the a bright light directly at the lens (unless you like lens flare).  This is one reason I tried to diffuse the light a bit.<br/> <br/>The first step of the process is lighting the scene - that involves keeping the light itself out of the frame - and not lighting anything you don''t want to see.  The cool thing about having a moving lightsource is that you can light up areas that may otherwise be in shadow -so you can get a hyper-real effect sometimes.<br/> <br/>The part where the "paint" is the light itself is just trial and error and keep in mind where the camera is in relation to your subject.  Timing is essential though and having a steady hand helps too.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Citadel:</b></div><hr/><i> I really like when my early predictions are accurate. Congrats on the blue! I''d like to hear more about how you painted this. (like what angle etc)<br/> <br/>Well done! </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-26 13:59:49.</i></td>', 'First of all: Avoid pointing the a bright light directly at the lens (unless you like lens flare).  This is one reason I tried to diffuse the light a bit. The first step of the process is lighting the scene - that involves keeping the light itself out of the frame - and not lighting anything you don''t want to see.  The cool thing about having a moving lightsource is that you can light up areas that may otherwise be in shadow -so you can get a hyper-real effect sometimes. The part where the "paint" is the light itself is just trial and error and keep in mind where the camera is in relation to your subject.  Timing is essential though and having a steady hand helps too. Originally posted by Citadel: I really like when my early predictions are accurate. Congrats on the blue! I''d like to hear more about how you painted this. (like what angle etc) Well done! ', '2008-09-26 14:07:23.000000', '2008-09-26 14:59:49.000000', 0),
(4976840, 721904, 9462, '<td valign="top">I think this is telling you to start doing more nature shots.</td>', 'I think this is telling you to start doing more nature shots.', '2008-09-26 14:26:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4976866, 722768, 66384, '<td valign="top">You almost got the ''Momentary Lapse of Sucking'' punishment! Hard to believe this was straight from the camera -- the color, focus, and exposure are all so perfect. I really like the colors and the reflections. Thanks for sharing the camera settings.</td>', 'You almost got the ''Momentary Lapse of Sucking'' punishment! Hard to believe this was straight from the camera -- the color, focus, and exposure are all so perfect. I really like the colors and the reflections. Thanks for sharing the camera settings.', '2008-09-26 14:53:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4976939, 722475, 66384, '<td valign="top">Oooo, this is what I like!! I gave it a 9. I wish more people agreed with me. It doesn''t make me dizzy at all -- probably because I am not trying to bring it into focus. I just enjoy the lines, colors, shades and general composition -- all of which I like.</td>', 'Oooo, this is what I like!! I gave it a 9. I wish more people agreed with me. It doesn''t make me dizzy at all -- probably because I am not trying to bring it into focus. I just enjoy the lines, colors, shades and general composition -- all of which I like.', '2008-09-26 15:50:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4976956, 722487, 66384, '<td valign="top">Great idea, Peter, and well done. You''ve done variations of The Scream before. Is there something you are trying to tell us? :/</td>', 'Great idea, Peter, and well done. You''ve done variations of The Scream before. Is there something you are trying to tell us? :/', '2008-09-26 16:01:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4976962, 722865, 66384, '<td valign="top">Nice muted colors. The crop feels a bit off to me -- lime a bit too centered and bottom edge snipped off. But I like the image as a whole.</td>', 'Nice muted colors. The crop feels a bit off to me -- lime a bit too centered and bottom edge snipped off. But I like the image as a whole.', '2008-09-26 16:07:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4976975, 722802, 66384, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition and the colors. Now that the challenge is over, I hope you will give it some adjustments to bring out the colors more and increase the contrast. There is <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=828493" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">a thread</a> for showing before and after editing for this challenge.</td>', 'I really like the composition and the colors. Now that the challenge is over, I hope you will give it some adjustments to bring out the colors more and increase the contrast. There is a thread for showing before and after editing for this challenge.', '2008-09-26 16:12:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4976987, 722717, 66384, '<td valign="top">Very interesting effect and nice composition. I like ''Feet2'' also, but I think this composition, with the position of the train, is better. What I think is particularly interesting about this shot is seeing the man following the high heels.</td>', 'Very interesting effect and nice composition. I like ''Feet2'' also, but I think this composition, with the position of the train, is better. What I think is particularly interesting about this shot is seeing the man following the high heels.', '2008-09-26 16:17:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977051, 721382, 81530, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot. One of my top 5 votes.</td>', 'Awesome shot. One of my top 5 votes.', '2008-09-26 17:00:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977062, 721382, 28742, '<td valign="top">The effort alone deserves a gold ribbon! Well done!</td>', 'The effort alone deserves a gold ribbon! Well done!', '2008-09-26 17:07:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977110, 722920, 64568, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot and well deserved blue ;-)</td>', 'Wonderful shot and well deserved blue ;-)', '2008-09-26 17:48:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977122, 722725, 66384, '<td valign="top">Interesting stormy effect by the long exposure. It makes the weather look very foggy and/or rainy. The stationary railing gives the feeling of safety on this side while there is danger on the other side.</td>', 'Interesting stormy effect by the long exposure. It makes the weather look very foggy and/or rainy. The stationary railing gives the feeling of safety on this side while there is danger on the other side.', '2008-09-26 17:54:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977131, 722786, 66384, '<td valign="top">Lovely colors and contrast and nice crisp focus. I love the reflections. It feels a bit tilted, though.</td>', 'Lovely colors and contrast and nice crisp focus. I love the reflections. It feels a bit tilted, though.', '2008-09-26 17:58:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977156, 722861, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like the light and sharp focus on the blossoms. The composition doesn''t feel comfortable for me, though. I wish I could say why, but as hard as I have tried, I can''t put a finger on the reason.</td>', 'I like the light and sharp focus on the blossoms. The composition doesn''t feel comfortable for me, though. I wish I could say why, but as hard as I have tried, I can''t put a finger on the reason.', '2008-09-26 18:04:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977159, 722837, 68504, '<td valign="top">Thanks voters and commenters.  Especially to <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=66384" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">JuliBoc</a>.  And to <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67152" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bassbone</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=23002" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">basssman7</a> for their responses to my pms. (<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=40718" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">DrAchoo</a> acknowledged my 1/2 second but didn''t think it was an obvious enough long exposure, and I may have to agree, although the obvious is not high on my list of desiderata). <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=1158" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Jac</a> has responded by telling me how to take the same picture at a longer exposure (ISO 100, f 2.8) which indeed I may try the next time it comes up, although I expect some noise, and this was a minimal editing challenge, and the best (most noiseless) moon I have ever shot, and I doubt this would have happened had I not tried for the longest exposure via f8 and ISO 50.<br/> <br/>Okay, so I enjoyed the presumption of the higher end camera users, as well as the many submissions that exploited the possibilities of the challenge way more than mine.</td>', 'Thanks voters and commenters.  Especially to  JuliBoc.  And to  bassbone and  basssman7 for their responses to my pms. ( DrAchoo acknowledged my 1/2 second but didn''t think it was an obvious enough long exposure, and I may have to agree, although the obvious is not high on my list of desiderata).  Jac has responded by telling me how to take the same picture at a longer exposure (ISO 100, f 2.8) which indeed I may try the next time it comes up, although I expect some noise, and this was a minimal editing challenge, and the best (most noiseless) moon I have ever shot, and I doubt this would have happened had I not tried for the longest exposure via f8 and ISO 50. Okay, so I enjoyed the presumption of the higher end camera users, as well as the many submissions that exploited the possibilities of the challenge way more than mine.', '2008-09-26 18:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977166, 721755, 66384, '<td valign="top">I didn''t realize the background was books, but I like the way their colors radiate up from the clock. That continues the radiant nature of the clock as created by the zoom. I like this effect. The color of the image is strong and warm too. Very pleasing.</td>', 'I didn''t realize the background was books, but I like the way their colors radiate up from the clock. That continues the radiant nature of the clock as created by the zoom. I like this effect. The color of the image is strong and warm too. Very pleasing.', '2008-09-26 18:09:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977168, 722837, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think this is quite gorgeous.  I also think it would make a marvelous print.  I love (LOVE) that the treeline is just barely there, but *there*, and so crisp and clean.  And it is indeed one of the sharpest moon shots I''ve seen.  My fancy pants camera doesn''t get the moon nearly that cleanly, I''ll have you know.  And I quite get a kick out of the fact this isn''t edited.  :-)</td>', 'I think this is quite gorgeous.  I also think it would make a marvelous print.  I love (LOVE) that the treeline is just barely there, but *there*, and so crisp and clean.  And it is indeed one of the sharpest moon shots I''ve seen.  My fancy pants camera doesn''t get the moon nearly that cleanly, I''ll have you know.  And I quite get a kick out of the fact this isn''t edited.  :-)', '2008-09-26 18:10:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977315, 722224, 8891, '<td valign="top">Hi! Great colors and shot. Congrats on your top 20 finish. The building is part of the University of the Arts Campus on South Broad Street which is also known as the Avenue of the Arts. I think a building up by Pine Street, behind you in this shot, also was being lit with colored lights and also patterns earlier in the year. I have not noticed it recently. Congrats again!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-26 19:01:18.</i></td>', 'Hi! Great colors and shot. Congrats on your top 20 finish. The building is part of the University of the Arts Campus on South Broad Street which is also known as the Avenue of the Arts. I think a building up by Pine Street, behind you in this shot, also was being lit with colored lights and also patterns earlier in the year. I have not noticed it recently. Congrats again!', '2008-09-26 19:58:02.000000', '2008-09-26 20:01:18.000000', 0),
(4977322, 722224, 82112, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by banmorn:</b></div><hr/><i> Hi! Great colors and shot. Congrats on your top 20 finish. The building is part of the University of the Arts Campus on South Broad Street which is also known as the Avenue of the Arts. I think a building up by Pine Street, behind you in this shot, also was being lit with colored lights and also patterns earlier in the year. I have not noticed it recently. Congrats again! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Bob for filling in that blank and for your nice comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by banmorn: Hi! Great colors and shot. Congrats on your top 20 finish. The building is part of the University of the Arts Campus on South Broad Street which is also known as the Avenue of the Arts. I think a building up by Pine Street, behind you in this shot, also was being lit with colored lights and also patterns earlier in the year. I have not noticed it recently. Congrats again!   Thanks Bob for filling in that blank and for your nice comments.', '2008-09-26 20:04:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4977347, 722768, 48228, '<td valign="top">This is an awesome image straight from the camera. You did really well Brian, especially the soft hues in the wonderful blue colors. I am also very pleased it received some excellent comments, and I feel it deserved just a tad higher in the score, as I feel it deserved a 6 for sure. Well done, and as Deb says, you really do know your camera.</td>', 'This is an awesome image straight from the camera. You did really well Brian, especially the soft hues in the wonderful blue colors. I am also very pleased it received some excellent comments, and I feel it deserved just a tad higher in the score, as I feel it deserved a 6 for sure. Well done, and as Deb says, you really do know your camera.', '2008-09-26 20:48:22.000000', NULL, 0),
